  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual message as the target of the stereotype",
  "description": "The user is implicitly projected onto the textual message 'farmersonly.com... where white trash meet other white trash' as the intended audience or as the group being stereotyped. The meme positions the viewer as someone who either belongs to or is meant to understand the 'white trash' group being mocked, or as someone who is being invited to join or judge this group. There are no explicit deictics like 'you' or 'me', but the framing of the website as a gathering place for 'white trash' creates an implicit projection where the user is seen as part of the social group being described or as the one who would recognize the stereotype.",
